WEBVTT

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:19.210
There isn't much we know about the BETA.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:27.210
And what we do know was brought to us at the 
cost of many of our forebearer's lives.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:34.340
That's why you need to make sure you listen 
to every word of this next lecture.

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:40.100
<b>Human  Soldier  Warrior Destroyer Fort Tank</b>

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:41.890
First, their ability to detect humans.

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:46.230
Hey, want to invite 
Yamashiro-san to lunch today?

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:47.710
The rule of thumb to use 
is that the bigger the BETA,

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:50.730
She wouldn't come.  
She's Yui's rival right?

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:50.650
the less likely it is to 
respond to an individual person.

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:51.890
Aww, come on.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:54.350
This means the smaller BETA

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:55.470
But maybe Yamashiro-san 
wants to make friends?

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:57.220
are in fact more dangerous 
to a normal person.

00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:00.490
I don't think she's that bad a person.

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:01.480
This means the Soldier class,

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:03.420
Yeah.

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:07.740
and the Tank class, who are 
the most common of the BETA.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:06.260
We're all gonna fight the BETA together.

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:11.170
If you encounter either of them

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:11.090
What's up, Yui?

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:18.250
Will there be a day when we 
look back on this time fondly?

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:14.040
without a TSF or an Enhanced Exoskeleton,

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.320
there's no hope for you to win.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:19.970
Run away as fast as you can!

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:55.020
<b>The End of a Deadly Battle</b>

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:07.200
I forgot my stuffed animal!

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.750
Give it up.

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:12.940
Sempai, Lt. Takamura isn't on 
this helicopter, it looks like.

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:16.000
She's not on the helicopter behind us?

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:20.140
I haven't been able to get 
to Argos Flight since then.

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:21.850
What's going on?

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:26.510
Yeah, something powerful has been jamming 
all communications around this area.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:28.250
Jamming?

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:31.200
Is there some new species that's 
capable of electronic warfare?

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:33.450
The BETA are jamming us?

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:35.230
No way.

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:36.650
Damn it!

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:41.360
Calm down.  Communications are 
coming back online gradually.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:45.390
We'll make contact with Kamchatsky base 
soon, and that's where we're landing.

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:47.040
Gradually?

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:53.970
Which means the jamming's coming 
from the frontline base.

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:55.920
And if that's not the BETA...

00:03:57.340 --> 00:04:00.180
What's going on back there?

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:10.600
<b>D-04 Frontline Supply Base Hangar 18</b>

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:15.350
What do I do?

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:18.230
What do I do?

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:22.370
He never gave up no matter how hard it got.

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:25.220
Yuuya Bridges...

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:29.050
Why am I thinking about 
him at a time like this?

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.720
Come on!  Come on!

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:19.180
Come on, damn it!

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:21.490
Corporal, move!

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:38.860
Lieutenant, you saved me.

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:40.320
You saved me.

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:42.230
Thank you, Corporal.

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:47.320
There's Tank class here already?

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:50.400
It won't be too long before 
they arrive en masse.

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:14.940
Unfortunately, it looks like I 
used all the ammo from that rifle.

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:17.010
You know how to use that gun, right?

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:21.660
Yes.  But these guns won't work on a Tank.

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:23.780
We might be shooting more than BETA.

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:28.400
When our mission is complete 
use it without hesitation.

00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:30.980
I will as well.

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:33.130
Lieutenant?

00:06:33.130 --> 00:06:34.330
Don't worry.

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:38.850
I'm not letting them get me 
until we finish our mission.

00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:40.840
Right, Corporal?

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:42.220
Yes.

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:44.680
Are the explosives ready?

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:46.220
Everything's set.

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:48.800
I've done everything I can.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:55.390
Good.  Now open the hatch so I can 
get to the cannon's core modules.

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:58.080
What are you going to do?

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:01.310
The BETA's highest target priority

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:04.500
is the combination of a 
powerful computer and a human.

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:06.600
You can't-

00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:12.530
I'll lure the BETA into destroying the 
EM Radiation Cannon's core modules.

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:32.170
It's no good.

00:07:32.170 --> 00:07:34.890
It's made of tougher stuff 
than your average safe.

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:37.700
You took it off for overauls, right?

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:42.980
That part's classified, so it's not 
part of the normal maintenance routine.

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:46.770
These defenses are made by the 
infamous Yokohama Company.

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:51.680
If a single mechanic could get through 
them, the brass would be pretty upset.

00:07:53.190 --> 00:07:56.980
Electronics are your speciality.  
I'm counting on you.

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:02.650
You only get one shot at life.

00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:06.650
There's nothing wrong with taking 
on a big challenge when it counts.

00:08:06.650 --> 00:08:07.770
I see.

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:11.650
Um... Lieutenant?

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:12.950
What?

00:08:14.020 --> 00:08:16.930
You said you were going to lure 
the BETA into the Core Module.

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:19.330
Would you let me do it?

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:22.560
No, I must be the one to do that.

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:23.960
But Lieutenant?

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:26.380
The military always prioritizes 
keeping its officers alive,

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:27.280
because that's what makes sense...

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:28.690
Corporal Yamamoto.

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:30.730
Don't stop working.

00:08:31.830 --> 00:08:35.920
Even as part of the UN I'm still 
a soldier of the Imperial Guard.

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:38.520
We're always leading the way and 
setting an example for the others.

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:43.160
Whether it makes sense or not, that is the 
responsibility of someone born into a Samurai Family.

00:08:45.650 --> 00:08:46.680
But...

00:08:47.090 --> 00:08:49.680
I'm a man.

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:57.610
I want my death to mean something, 
like dying to protect a woman.

00:08:57.610 --> 00:08:58.530
Corporal.

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:03.250
I'm sorry, Lieutenant.

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:04.490
I shouldn't have said that.

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:07.200
I'm a disgrace to the 
Imperial Military, aren't I?

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:11.840
Keep working.

00:09:12.230 --> 00:09:14.090
I'll keep watch.

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:28.460
<b>50 km behind D-04 Frontline Supply Base</b>

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:39.810
Interference in effect around 
D-04 Frontline Supply Base.

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:42.730
Communications with the affected 
area have been completely cut off.

00:09:42.730 --> 00:09:46.100
BETA group 7 scouts have entered the base.

00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:50.100
The frontline base is completely cut off now.

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:55.080
A BETA attacked and a mysterious 
communications jam.

00:09:56.930 --> 00:09:59.830
Real combat is a terrifying thing.

00:09:59.830 --> 00:10:02.620
You never know what will happen.

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:08.680
But that supply base is the lynchpin 
of the Kamchatsky defense line.

00:10:08.680 --> 00:10:11.740
I'd like to minimize damage to it.

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:14.130
What's Zhar Battalion doing?

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:17.260
Moving towards the supply base.

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:19.790
They'll soon enter the interference area.

00:10:19.790 --> 00:10:21.120
Will you contact them?

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:26.140
No.  They're veterans of many 
battles, we can trust them.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:32.900
Trust that they'll eliminate the 
BETA and protect the supply base.

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:38.040
And recover what was left behind there.

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:03.670
We have to do something soon, 
or our deaths will mean nothing.

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:11.180
I want my death to mean something, 
like dying to protect a woman.

00:11:12.310 --> 00:11:15.820
After all this I'm still 
being treated like a woman.

00:11:17.810 --> 00:11:18.550
Lieu-

00:11:21.600 --> 00:11:22.790
Corporal, what's wrong?

00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:24.170
It's fine.

00:11:24.170 --> 00:11:25.320
I'll go take a look.

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:27.630
Corporal, wait!

00:11:57.730 --> 00:11:59.360
Oww...

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:50.130
Corporal Yamamoto!

00:12:51.110 --> 00:12:53.570
Lieutenant, save me!

00:13:01.390 --> 00:13:02.600
Ru-

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:09.600
It hurts!  It hurts!

00:13:32.840 --> 00:13:37.010
You did well, Corporal Yamamoto.

00:14:10.130 --> 00:14:13.000
I won't make another mistake.

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:15.480
I won't run from my decision ever again.

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:27.500
And I will accept the results of my choice.

00:15:13.250 --> 00:15:16.030
Please, forgive me.

00:15:16.910 --> 00:15:19.630
Please forgive me...

00:15:32.150 --> 00:15:33.160
Father...

00:15:34.520 --> 00:15:39.160
Forgive me for dying without 
completing my task.

00:15:51.210 --> 00:15:52.980
Yuuya...

00:15:56.090 --> 00:15:56.980
What?

00:16:12.520 --> 00:16:13.340
Yuuya?

00:16:21.930 --> 00:16:23.430
What are you doing here?

00:16:23.840 --> 00:16:24.740
You moron!

00:16:29.140 --> 00:16:31.460
What are you thinking staying here alone?

00:16:31.460 --> 00:16:33.880
What are you thinking?

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:35.980
Nobody issued an order to rescue me.

00:16:36.370 --> 00:16:38.050
Sure, nobody did.

00:16:38.050 --> 00:16:44.010
But nobody told you to stay 
behind to destroy this thing!

00:16:46.370 --> 00:16:47.560
Anyway, let's hurry.

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:50.960
Hey, are you okay?

00:16:51.450 --> 00:16:52.730
You're pushing yourself too hard.

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:56.220
It doesn't matter what happens to me.

00:16:56.220 --> 00:16:57.440
Shut up.

00:16:57.440 --> 00:17:00.600
You're the one who told me that people 
are more important than equipment.

00:17:01.130 --> 00:17:02.710
Was that a lie?

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:04.750
It wasn't...

00:17:05.050 --> 00:17:08.420
Then we can't lose you either!

00:17:12.740 --> 00:17:15.700
Weren't you going to make 
the XFJ project a success?

00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:22.700
I don't know what you're trying to martyr 
yourself for, but I can't lose you now.

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:30.340
I was always taught never 
to leave a man behind.

00:17:30.930 --> 00:17:32.950
So I won't abandon you.

00:17:33.830 --> 00:17:34.950
Ever.

00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:39.450
What are those two doing?

00:17:43.770 --> 00:17:46.050
You shouldn't bother them right now.

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:52.690
There's no end to them.

00:17:52.690 --> 00:17:57.090
I really don't want to be wasting 
ammunition or fuel right now.

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:03.150
Oh my.

00:18:03.630 --> 00:18:06.100
Send the bill to the UN, okay?

00:18:13.940 --> 00:18:16.130
Argos 1 to Argos 4!

00:18:16.130 --> 00:18:17.100
What was that?

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:19.770
Just a nice little campfire.

00:18:20.210 --> 00:18:22.090
More importantly, what about Lt. Takamura?

00:18:22.610 --> 00:18:24.090
I've got her.

00:18:24.460 --> 00:18:26.980
I'm giving her first-aid for her wounds.

00:18:26.980 --> 00:18:28.640
Hurry, Argos 1.

00:18:28.640 --> 00:18:30.590
The enemy's main force is almost here.

00:18:30.910 --> 00:18:32.730
Roger, Argos 4.

00:18:32.730 --> 00:18:36.010
We'll be out of here in 
15 minutes, per the plan.

00:18:36.270 --> 00:18:38.020
The interference here is awful.

00:18:38.460 --> 00:18:41.220
These radios are made to work 
in a heavy metal cloud too.

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:43.320
They'll only work at this distance.

00:18:43.710 --> 00:18:49.480
Well, the Soviets left this place in a 
hurry, so some kind of human error probably.

00:18:49.740 --> 00:18:50.900
Roger.

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:52.700
Leave the com line open.

00:18:53.090 --> 00:18:55.840
As soon as I've finished applying 
first aid we're out of here.

00:18:56.130 --> 00:18:57.580
Argos 4, roger.

00:18:58.020 --> 00:19:00.800
I'll continue monitoring the area.

00:19:01.930 --> 00:19:03.440
You heard her.

00:19:03.440 --> 00:19:04.480
There's no time.

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:06.790
Ready?

00:19:07.220 --> 00:19:08.850
Yeah, thanks.

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:13.590
Grab onto my arm.

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:16.040
Just do it.

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:17.970
Right.

00:19:25.270 --> 00:19:25.870
Okay.

00:19:34.630 --> 00:19:35.810
That'll do it.

00:19:35.810 --> 00:19:36.820
Good job.

00:19:38.060 --> 00:19:41.130
I'm surprised how tough you are.

00:19:41.790 --> 00:19:43.830
Don't make fun of me.

00:19:46.110 --> 00:19:50.520
Just to make sure, you didn't 
bring the whole Flight did you?

00:19:50.520 --> 00:19:52.210
Yeah, it's just us.

00:19:53.060 --> 00:19:57.290
The Active used a lot of 
fuel in the exercises.

00:19:57.290 --> 00:19:59.580
They just gave us their 
weapons and spare ammo.

00:19:59.950 --> 00:20:03.300
For better or for worse, 
since we were chasers

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:07.600
the 94 Second and Strike 
both had lots of fuel left.

00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:08.600
I see.

00:20:10.190 --> 00:20:14.490
Yuuya got Lt. Takamura out okay, right?

00:20:14.790 --> 00:20:16.000
I don't know.

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:19.040
The interference is really bad, and I 
haven't been able to get a hold of them.

00:20:19.790 --> 00:20:23.950
But if this jamming was deliberate...

00:20:24.260 --> 00:20:25.440
Deliberate?

00:20:25.440 --> 00:20:26.440
The Soviets?

00:20:27.130 --> 00:20:30.180
It might have something 
to do with the fact that

00:20:30.180 --> 00:20:32.250
they didn't seal the holes 
the BETA made a month ago.

00:20:33.160 --> 00:20:36.070
Then we have to go too!

00:20:36.070 --> 00:20:38.010
We don't know what could happen!

00:20:38.260 --> 00:20:40.590
Don't be stupid, sensei.

00:20:40.590 --> 00:20:44.800
There's barely enough fuel 
left to get us to Kamchatsky.

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:45.770
Damn it!

00:20:45.770 --> 00:20:48.280
I should've brought extra tanks!

00:20:48.280 --> 00:20:51.800
It's fine.  Stella will take care of it.

00:20:51.800 --> 00:20:53.600
We have to believe in her.

00:20:56.070 --> 00:21:00.470
But I've just got a bad feeling.

00:21:01.370 --> 00:21:02.930
Okay, that does it.

00:21:03.610 --> 00:21:07.450
Now let's do it before the BETA get here.

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:09.360
Do what?

00:21:09.360 --> 00:21:10.680
What else?

00:21:11.520 --> 00:21:13.130
Get him out of here.

00:21:14.140 --> 00:21:15.570
I told you, didn't I?

00:21:15.570 --> 00:21:17.490
That I wouldn't leave it behind.

00:21:18.850 --> 00:21:21.490
I know the position you're in.

00:21:21.930 --> 00:21:26.750
If it was functional we 
could've wiped out the BETA.

00:21:27.130 --> 00:21:29.910
Well, too late for that now.

00:21:29.910 --> 00:21:32.220
It's a shame the mount arm's off,

00:21:32.220 --> 00:21:34.850
but if the 94 Second and Strike carry it...

00:21:34.850 --> 00:21:36.010
There's no need for that.

00:21:37.020 --> 00:21:39.530
I won't run from my decision anymore.

00:21:40.280 --> 00:21:43.350
I can't let the Type 99 cannon 
I brought here to keep him alive

00:21:43.350 --> 00:21:45.370
turn into a huge risk.

00:21:45.370 --> 00:21:46.540
That would defeat the point.

00:21:47.340 --> 00:21:49.540
Are you sure?

00:21:50.250 --> 00:21:52.020
Per the original plan,

00:21:52.650 --> 00:21:57.530
we'll destroy the Type 99 EM 
Radiation Cannon prototype here.

00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:10.250
What?  What's going on?

00:22:11.740 --> 00:22:15.640
All the BETA are heading for this hangar!

00:24:07.380 --> 00:24:11.340
Am I forced to just stand 
by and watch once more?

00:24:12.520 --> 00:24:15.520
I swore I wouldn't cry anymore...

00:24:16.460 --> 00:24:18.210
I've endured so much...

00:24:17.140 --> 00:24:24.480
<b>The Price of a Choice</b>

00:24:19.720 --> 00:24:22.210
Next time on Total Eclipse:

00:24:22.210 --> 00:24:23.940
The Price of a Choice
